# Imported Visible World

- Every visible physical production object or surface must be an imported GLB
  and/or imported/generated texture from the project asset pipeline.
- Do not build visible buildings, ground, roads, barriers, traversal props,
  furniture, signs, clutter, interiors, or backdrop fabric from Three/React
  primitive or procedural geometry.
- Missing/loading physical assets render nothing and fail QA; never substitute
  a visible primitive fallback or debug shell in production.
- Runtime code may transform, animate, instance, or shade imported assets.
- Procedural code is allowed for invisible collision, portals, triggers,
  navigation, dev diagnostics, UI/Archive highlights, sky, fog, animated water,
  weather, lighting, particles, shaders, and contact shadows.
- New physical assets follow Gemini concept → visual/historical QA → Meshy →
  scoped Blender optimization → verification manifest → targeted web sync.
- Keep west/southwest harbor water open; never extend backdrop city or land
  surfaces into the harbor exclusion bands documented in World-Design-Bible.
